cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use judge-check in your research, please cite it as below. If you
  report results on the built-in demo corpus, please also cite HotpotQA (listed
  under references).
type: software
title: "judge-check: measuring how far you can trust an LLM judge in RAG evaluation"
abstract: >-
  judge-check measures the reliability of the LLM judge in a RAG evaluation
  setup. It scores the judge against answer variants whose correctness is known
  by construction (deterministic mutations of correct answers), anchors the
  error rates to human adjudication, and reports false-accept and false-reject
  rates with bootstrap confidence intervals, together with the minimum accuracy
  difference that is interpretable given those error rates.
authors:
